          "worked": "Make one row for each of the two coins in bag 1 and one column for each of the five coins in bag 2. Label the columns 10, 10, 10, 50, 50 cents. The 10-cent row contains $(10,10)$ three times and $(10,50)$ twice. The 50-cent row contains $(50,10)$ three times and $(50,50)$ twice. There are $2\\times5=10$ equally likely cells, even though some value pairs repeat.",
